    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1234">

                <pb facs="1008" n="998" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg998"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 Ward, Angus I.: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul General at Peiping</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Clubb</hi>)<anchor n="35" xml:id="d1234-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-11-02T18:00:00-05:00">November 2, 1949—6
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>766. Dept considering instructing Moscow approach Sov FonOff outlining general
                    circumstances re ConGen Mukden and requesting Sovs exercise good offices
                    ascertain reasons continued Commie failure permit Ward and staff depart and to
                    facilitate departure. Ur comments wld be appreciated.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1234-f1" n="35" type="source" xml:id="d1234-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to the Ambassador in the Soviet Union as telegram No. 814.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
